<section id="portal-terms" class="mt-4 pt-3 border-top" aria-label="Portal terms of use">
    <h2 class="h5 fw-bold text-primary-drmc">Portal terms of use</h2>
    <h3 class="h6 fw-bold mt-3">Your account and information</h3>
    <p>Provide accurate details when registering, review information extracted from your ID, and correct any mistakes before submitting. Use your own identity documents and keep your password and verification codes private. Sign out when using a shared device.</p>
    <h3 class="h6 fw-bold mt-3">Using patient services</h3>
    <p>Use the portal to manage your own healthcare information and requests. Do not try to access another patient's account or records. Appointment, assistance, and refill requests remain subject to the hospital's review and available services; submitting a request does not guarantee approval.</p>
    <h3 class="h6 fw-bold mt-3">Medical care and emergencies</h3>
    <p>The portal supports your care and does not replace advice from your healthcare team. Discuss results and treatment questions with your clinician. For urgent symptoms or a medical emergency, seek immediate in-person care rather than waiting for a portal response.</p>
    <h3 class="h6 fw-bold mt-3">Privacy and your choice</h3>
    <p>Registration requires the processing described in the privacy notice, including identity verification and retention of any ID documents you submit. Contact the hospital using the details above for privacy questions or requests about your information. You can leave signup without accepting and continue to browse public information.</p>
</section>
